            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="COO01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <forename>Thomas </forename>
                        <surname>Cooper</surname>
                        <addName>Abthorpe</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1775-12-16">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1849-04-21"/>
                    <occupation>actor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Cooper was a cousin of Godwin's. When his father died, he was sent to
                            live with Godwin who undertook his education. Later he became an actor -
                            after the tutelage of <persName key="HOL01">Thomas Holcroft</persName>
                            and Godwin - and moved to America where he had much success. He
                            occasionally returned to England where he kept in contact with
                            Godwin.</p>
                        <p>Entries are assumed to be Thomas Cooper if they are T. Cooper, Cooper,
                            or, occasionally, C. In 1796 Cooper went to America. He returned for a
                            series of performances in March 1803 - November 1804. There are
                            correspondingly many entries for Cooper in these years, and a number for
                                <persName key="COO08">Mrs T Cooper</persName> and 3 Coopers (he
                            brought his family over in the summer of 1803). However, there are also
                            Cooper entries (2) in 1805, but as Thomas was at this time performing in
                            Boston, these refer to a different, unidentified Cooper. Also, there is
                            a T Cooper in 1809 and other Coopers in 1810, but the evidence suggests
                            that he does not return to Britain until July 1810 - Feb 1811 so most of
                            these are not coded. There is an aditional problem in that there are
                            occasional references to C in the Diary, which we take to refer to
                            Cooper - but a good number of these are in the period he is supposed to
                            be in America. These must be questionable attributions, although we
                            might also consider it possible that he went back and forth more easily
                            than we imagine. It is not clear who another intimate of Godwin's would
                            have usurped the shortened 'C'. Ed Pope, however, has a plausible discussion that has led us to re-code a range of these entries - on which see the other entry for Thomas Cooper - COO09)</p>
                    </note>
